  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In this step, you\u2019ll address the clutter in your Unity project's <b>Hierarchy</b> window caused by numerous <b>Block</b> prefabs. \n\nYou'll learn to organize these blocks under a single parent GameObject, simplifying your scene and making it more manageable. \n\nAs a reminder, a <b>parent</b> GameObject is a GameObject that serves as a container for other GameObjects, known as <b>child</b> GameObjects. These terms describe a hierarchical relationship, much like a family tree."
